Ordinary tokens get a negative onset value. Modal auxiliaries, negation,
stance/frequency adverbs and first-person subjects reverse its sign.
Comment openers and a few control/separator tokens have their own offsets.
After the initial token (or an initial run of one repeated token), predict
zero, except for the colon in a document-opening 'Title:' metadata field.
The constants are approximate training means, not token-ID lookups.
