"""Approximate a detector of repeated line-prefix formatting.

Track the current and previous lines. Comment prefixes, quote and diff
markers, and table bars respond at line starts. Matching comment prefixes
are stronger, especially after empty prefixed lines or decorative borders.
Indentation, spacing, and printed line numbers change their strengths.
Diff signs before comments are skipped when recognizing those comments.
Newline-fused markers are quiet except for an initial empty // line.
Non-breaking spaces after line numbers respond positively; initial digit
runs following dotted-leader lines respond negatively. Ordinary words and
other small, token-specific fluctuations are left near zero.
