  two of them), 一方 / 各方 / 多方 (one side / each party / many parties), 两国 (two
  countries), and 旁 / 岸 (beside, bank). These fire strongly.
- A group noun right after a count word 两 / 兩 / 双 / 雙 / 三 / 二, when the noun
  names a side, party, group or country (两者, 双方, 双人, 两国, 两派, 三军, 两代 ...).
  The noun after the count word fires; the count word itself does not.
- Rural words: 农村, 乡村, 城乡 (strong) and 村 (weaker).
- A number unit written directly after a digit, such as 20万, 5000万, 3亿, 7万亩:
  negative (万, 萬, 亿, 亩, 吨, 辆 and compounds).
- 对方 (the other party): weakly negative.
- Carriage-return characters \\r, which sit in long Windows-style blank runs: weakly positive.

